Xiong Jiao Man (also referred to as Xiong Jian Man) is the character who famously appears to die twice due to a continuity and plotting error in Reverend Insanity.

The Continuity Error Details

First Death (Chapter 189 in fandom, Chapter 197 in our raw): The character is seemingly decapitated by Bai Ning Bing during the clashes at Qing Mao Mountain clan conflicts. Raw Ch197: "熊群早已经全灭，甚至就连熊骄嫚也被白凝冰一刀枭首，娇丽的头颅飞出老远去，脖颈血喷如泉。" [Bear horde already completely annihilated, even Xiong Jiao Man was beheaded by Bai Ning Bing with one blade, her lovely head flew far away, neck blood sprayed like fountain.]

Second Death (Chapter 194 in fandom): Just five chapters later, she reappears active in the plot only to be killed yet again, creating a notable oversight by the author Gu Zhen Ren. In our raw edition 2342 files, we found only one death at Ch197, no second appearance after Ch197, 47 occurrences total Ch132-Ch197 only. So in this edition, she dies only once. The two deaths claim may be from different edition or fandom memory mixing.

Fandom post https://reverend-insanity.fandom.com/f/p/4400000000002358343 confirms: Is it for sure that she dies twice? Is it really confirmed that Xiong Jiao Man = Xiong Jian Man? Talking about chapters 189 and 194. Reply: Yes they are the same person, the name is the same down to the chinese characters. Yes Gu Zhen Ren doesn't give a flying fuck about a jobber whose job was to be decapitated by Bai Ning Bing and unknowingly revive her just to kill her again.

Our raw verification of Ch189 and Ch194: Ch189 is about Tie Ruo Nan deducing Fang Yuan is Ten Extreme, no Xiong Jiao Man death. Ch194 is about blood lake battle Gu Yue First Generation vs Tie Xue Leng and three clans pre selection, no Xiong Jiao Man death. So in our raw, Ch189 and Ch194 contain zero death of Xiong Jiao Man. Only Ch197 contains death.

How does defensive Gu save from decapitation: It cannot when raw says head flew far away and neck blood sprayed like fountain. That is complete severing, fatal. Defensive Gu like Bronze Skin can resist cuts but cannot reattach head after it flies far.

Our fixation: We will not use defensive Gu saves from decapitation. If we need continuity for two deaths claim from other edition, we will write first as near decapitation, severe wound, not complete severing, so survival plausible with healing Gu. In our edition where only Ch197 death exists, we keep that as final death, no second death.

Community Reception: Fans note because she is a minor side character, the continuity slip went unedited and uncorrected in final release.
